<!--
  Hand-maintained: the site is a fixed handful of pages, so generating this
  would be more machinery than it saves. Add an entry when you add a page.

  No <lastmod>: the map's data changes nightly but its markup does not, and a
  date that claims otherwise is worse than no date at all. <changefreq> and
  <priority> are omitted because Google ignores both.

  The xhtml:link alternates repeat what the pages' own hreflang tags say. That
  is the documented belt-and-braces — for the ?lang= views especially, the
  sitemap is the channel that does not depend on the crawler rendering JS.
-->
